    "entry_after": {
      "id": "C14",
      "title_zh": "生成对选择的递归影响",
      "title_en": "Recursive influence of generation on selection",
      "claim_zh": "活动后果可改变后继形成与下一轮选择条件，贡献变体不必获益。重构、发育、留存和聚合区分遗传群体与运输集合；细菌谱系及回复实验接通遗传切换和周期完成。时间遮蔽预测进一步支持实际谱系的信息作用，给常规贝叶斯解释完整信用。",
      "claim_en": "Consequences can change successor formation and later selection without guaranteeing contributor advantage. Reconstruction, development, retention and aggregation distinguish inherited clusters from transport groups; bacterial genealogy and reversion connect inherited switching to cycle completion. Chronological forecasts further support the information carried by ancestry, fully crediting conventional Bayesian explanation.",
